      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58738,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 55,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours form a nondescript mass at the dermal&ndash;subcutaneous junction, usually &lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;cm in size.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:46:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58739,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 55,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Plexiform fibrohistiocytic tumours are centred at the dermal&ndash;subcutaneous junction. They show an infiltrative architecture with overall plexiform outlines and may extend into skeletal muscle. The tumours are composed of small nodules of histiocytoid cells and osteoclast-like multinucleated giant cells, surrounded by fascicles of spindle cells in varying proportions. There may be haemorrhage, haemosiderin deposition, and a chronic inflammatory infiltrate. Lymphovascular invasion can rarely be seen. Additional rare findings include myxoid or hyalinized stromal changes and metaplastic bone formation. By immunohistochemistry, the spindle cells express SMA {22441367}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:46:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58740,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 55,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:46:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
